# CatMorph is a fully static site, so it doesn't need any server-side
# secrets at runtime. Visitors paste their own Replicate API token into the
# Settings panel, and it's stored in their browser's localStorage.
#
# The two variables below are only used at *build* time:

# Set this when building for a Pages site served at https://<user>.github.io/<repo>/.
# The deploy workflow sets it automatically to /<repo>; only set it locally
# if you want to preview the production basePath via `npm run build`.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/dev
